cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this course material, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "agent-lab: learning by doing, from the 1958 perceptron to multi-agent harnesses"
abstract: >-
  A hands-on course in nine chapters. Each chapter tells true stories from the history of
  machine learning and AI, lets you rebuild the key moment in code written from scratch
  (numpy or the Python standard library, runnable without an API key), and then explains
  the concepts. It goes from the perceptron and gradient descent to Transformers, LLM APIs,
  agent loops, harness engineering, multi-agent systems, and getting Claude, GPT and
  DeepSeek to work together through adapters and protocols such as MCP and A2A.
